/-!
# The forty-eight second cubics in a marked binary A₄ pair

With the first fixed-free A₄ normalized, a second cubic c satisfies
c³ = (r c)³ = 1 and has exactly one nonzero common fixed vector with r.
An exhaustive column calculation leaves forty-eight choices. The listed
frames normalize the first A₄ and carry each choice to (8,2,4,11).
The companion normal-form proof checks and interprets these frame identities.

Every matrix condition is reduced by Lean's kernel. External computations
supply only candidate tables, never a classification assumption. This is the
finite local calculation used for Aschbacher–Smith 14.3.19(4).
-/

